Description: No empty window while a document loads
 LibreOffice showed a document's window as soon as it was created, before
 the document was loaded into it, so for a second or more an empty frame
 stood on screen, titled only by the process (soffice.bin). Write and
 Tables show the Wild OS loading screen until the document is ready, so the
 window is now shown once the document is in it. The window is still the
 parent of any message the import raises.
Author: Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/framework/source/loadenv/loadenv.cxx
+++ b/framework/source/loadenv/loadenv.cxx
@@ -1138,12 +1138,10 @@
                 {"Parent", uno::Any(xWindow)}
             }));
             xHandler->initialize(aArguments);
-            //show the frame as early as possible to make it the parent of any message dialogs
-            if (!impl_filterHasInteractiveDialog())
-            {
-                impl_makeFrameWindowVisible(xWindow, shouldFocusAndToFront());
-                m_bFocusedAndToFront = true; // no need to ask shouldFocusAndToFront second time
-            }
+            // Wild OS: the window is not shown before the document is in it.
+            // Shown here it would stand empty, without a title, while the
+            // document loads; Write and Tables show their own loading screen
+            // until it is ready. Message dialogs still have it as parent.
         }
     }
 
